<title>BELGIUM: EU imposes dumping penalties on Asian cotton cloth.</title>
<headline>EU imposes dumping penalties on Asian cotton cloth.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had imposed provisional anti-dumping penalties averaging 20 percent on grey cotton fabric from India, China, Indonesia, Pakistan, Turkey and Egypt.</p>
<p>After an extensive investigation of 19 unnamed textile exporting companies in the countries concerned the Commission found &quot;clear evidence of dumping&quot;, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Such practice had caused material injury to the European Union industry in recent years, it concluded. &quot;Production, sales, employment and capacity have all declined.&quot;</p>
<p>The Commission said it was aware that the provisional measures, which take the form of guarantees rather than import duties, could harm industries that import grey cotton cloth in Europe to process it.</p>
<p>The Commission will carry an in-depth investigation on this and the other aspects of the case before deciding whether to make the dumping measures definitive.</p>
</text>
